{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And the man knew et</b> etc. — for relations." "<b>I have acquired a man et HaShem.</b> In the creation of the world — that is, from בראשית until אלה תולדות השמים — the Holy One, blessed be He, is mentioned only by the name Elohim, to say that He created His world with the attribute of justice. And in the making of the world and its ordering — that is, from אלה תולדות השמים until והאדם ידע — He is mentioned with two designations, to tell you that He joined the attribute of mercy with the attribute of justice, perhaps His world could endure. And do not object: even though it says 'אף כי אמר Elohim,' 'אשר בתוך הגן אמר Elohim,' 'כי יודע Elohim' — because these are the words of the serpent and Chava. And from והאדם ידע onward, when the evil inclination came and grows strong in creatures, the Holy One, blessed be He, withdrew His attribute of justice and is mentioned with the attribute of mercy alone, to conduct Himself with His creatures through it, in order to establish and sustain His world."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:02:52.912941986Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}